            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for understanding, then the Marathi for common sense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हट्टी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हट्टी — haṭṭī — \"stubborn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हट्टी बाळ खेळण्यासाठी रडत राहिलं. haṭṭī bāḷ kheḷṇyāsāṭhī raḍat rāhilaṁ. The stubborn baby kept crying for the toy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From हट्ट, insistence: हट्ट करणे, to insist like a child. Unchanging."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हट्टी (haṭṭī) is a Marathi adjective built on हट्ट, \"insistence\", which goes back to Sanskrit haṭha, \"force; obstinacy\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
